Skills Needed
1. SQL – Joins, CTEs, subqueries, aggregations, data validation.
2. Excel – Data reconciliation, Pivot Tables, lookup functions.
3. Power BI / Tableau – Data quality and financial reporting dashboards.
4. Data Warehousing – Fact tables, dimension tables, data marts, data mapping.
5. Accounting Basics – Debit, credit, ledger entries, balance reconciliation.
6. Data Quality – Missing values, duplicates, mismatched records, validation rules.
7. Root Cause Analysis – Investigating why numbers differ between systems.
8. Documentation – Data dictionaries, business rules and SQL logic.
Introduction
This project simulates a real banking data warehouse environment where financial data comes from multiple source systems, including customer accounts, transactions, and accounting ledgers.

Using SQL, Excel, and Power BI, the project will build a simplified banking data mart, reconcile transaction records against accounting ledger entries, identify discrepancies, detect duplicate and missing records, and establish data quality validation rules.

The goal is to ensure financial data is accurate, consistent, and reliable for management reporting, accounting operations, and regulatory reporting.
